WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.690
Before we get started, we wanna remind you

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:05.840
that this is the last episode
before we take three weeks off

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.040
so three week break,
opportunity for you to listen

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.931
to some older Ear Biscuits,
maybe one you missed

00:00:09.931 --> 00:00:11.820
or your favorite one.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.370
And we'll be back on August 19th,

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:17.162
right after we get back
from our big vacations

00:00:17.162 --> 00:00:20.053
that we will fill you in all about.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:26.060
Welcome to Ear Biscuits, I'm Rhett.

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:27.390
And I'm Link.

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:30.757
This week at the round
table of dim lighting,

00:00:30.757 --> 00:00:34.060
we ask the question are we too nice?

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:35.510
Hmm.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:38.670
Are we too nice?
You mean like Too Nice,

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:42.290
like the old, wasn't there
a musician named Too Nice?

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:44.200
There was a rapper named D-Nice.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:45.620
Ah, there wasn't a Too Nice

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:48.040
with like a Too and then a Nice?

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:49.473
My name is D-Nice.

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:52.470
I remember your brother owned that CD.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:53.650
I thought that was Denice.

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:57.010
And it wasn't that memorable.

00:00:57.010 --> 00:00:58.980
See, Jacob said there was a Too Nice.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:00.680
There's also a Too Nice?

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:04.340
Well look up D-Nice because the letter D,

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:07.580
the space which is a space
and then the word Nice.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:09.930
'Cause Too Nice doesn't
sound like a cool name

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:11.730
for a musician.

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:12.620
You don't wanna be too nice--

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:13.770
D dash Nice.

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:15.490
D dash Nice.
D dash Nice.

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:19.576
Oh I know, Cole had that
CD and I'd go into his room

00:01:19.576 --> 00:01:21.310
when I was going over to your house.

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:23.250
He had it all.
Hanging out with you.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.050
You didn't even have a CD player.

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:29.130
He had a CD player,
man, and he had rap CDs

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:31.200
and I'd go in there and I'd listen to him.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.060
I'd listen to them.
Listen to him.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:35.229
Well I'd listen to him talk about his CDs

00:01:35.229 --> 00:01:37.890
and occasionally he'd play them.

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:40.090
He had much better music
taste than you did.

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:42.040
Well he was, I think he also was--

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:43.050
It's the older brother syndrome.

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:45.290
Older brother, yeah, it's
like I technically had access

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:46.550
to his library.

00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:49.002
I knew it was all being handed
down to me at some point.

00:01:49.002 --> 00:01:49.835
Yeah but you couldn't play it though

00:01:49.835 --> 00:01:52.210
because you didn't have a CD player.

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:53.611
I eventually had a CD player.

00:01:53.611 --> 00:01:55.330
Of course eventually you did.

00:01:55.330 --> 00:01:57.850
But I had a tape player for a long time.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:01:59.820
There was a weird moment
when he transitioned

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:03.250
to CDs where I was a little
bit left in the dark.

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:05.760
But also we had thin walls in the house

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:09.200
and we shared a wall so I kind of listened

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:10.793
to muffled D-Nice.

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:13.680
Did you ever talk to him through the wall?

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:16.670
I mean I never, I know this is
not what we're talking about

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:17.670
but we're talking about it.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:20.758
This relates to my dream .

00:02:20.758 --> 00:02:22.100
It's kinda funny.
Your dream?

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.780
I have to tell you the dream
I had that you were in.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:26.710
All right so we're gonna
talk about are we too nice.

00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:27.780
It is a question that
we've asked ourselves--

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.420
I did talk to him.
And each other many times--

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:30.560
Through the wall.
But first your dream.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:33.360
I yelled at him through
the wall and vice versa.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.320
Shut up!

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.350
That kinda thing, you know.

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:36.183
That's ironic.

00:02:36.183 --> 00:02:40.654
But there was no prison
sort of communication

00:02:40.654 --> 00:02:42.760
between the two walls.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.050
And the reason I say prison is

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:46.839
because that's what my dream was about

00:02:46.839 --> 00:02:50.050
and I believe and my wife pointed this out

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:51.130
when I told her about this dream.

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:53.780
She said the reason you
dreamed this is because

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:58.240
of that question that we got
in the live LTAT at VidCon

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:01.140
where the question was who
would survive better in prison?

00:03:03.274 --> 00:03:05.120
And your answer was not me.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:08.810
I just said I don't think
Linky Poo would do too well.

00:03:09.671 --> 00:03:10.553
In prison.
In prison.

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:13.920
I didn't know what you meant by that.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.000
I think most people do.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.950
That wasn't very nice.

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:19.410
Yeah I'm not Too Nice, man.

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:20.473
I'm D-Nice.

00:03:22.505 --> 00:03:27.505
Okay so I had a dream
that you were in prison

00:03:27.688 --> 00:03:30.650
and you were in prison--

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:33.180
For murder.
Oh crap.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:34.810
I knew no details.

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:38.180
All I knew is that you
had been falsely accused.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:39.013
Oh good.

00:03:39.013 --> 00:03:40.470
And I don't know if it
was because I just knew

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:43.910
in your character so well
that you're not capable

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:46.820
of murder but I just
think that the pretense--

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:49.120
Don't think Linky Poo's capable of murder.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:52.830
The pretense in the dream
was that I was going

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:54.770
to talk to you about how we were going

00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:58.623
to get you out legally, not
break you out but I was like,

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:02.240
this is a false accusation so

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:07.240
for some reason the
prison was in Keith Hills.

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:11.890
So the golf course,
the gated neighborhood,

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:16.030
slash golf course that was
next to where we both grew up

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:16.863
in Buies Creek.

00:04:16.863 --> 00:04:18.760
That we're going to next week.

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:20.310
We're going to visit and--

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:22.220
So all this is on your mind.
Yes.

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:24.925
Maybe there is a, I know they
expanded the golf course.

00:04:24.925 --> 00:04:28.227
I have not heard that they added a prison.

00:04:28.227 --> 00:04:32.550
Well golfers can be very,
very disorderly sometimes.

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:34.110
They break clubs and
stuff, it would be nice

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:36.270
to have a detention center for them.

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:38.740
So you were on your way to the prison

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:40.103
which was in the golf course.

00:04:40.103 --> 00:04:42.193
I got, no, I was at the prison.

00:04:43.503 --> 00:04:46.860
And the prison was near the river.

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:49.555
The prison was basically where
we're going to be next week,

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:52.930
in that area where Cinder
Morgan's old house was.

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:57.697
Okay.
And so I go

00:04:57.697 --> 00:05:01.550
and my mission is to
talk to you about like,

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:03.430
dude we've gotta get a lawyer.

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:07.230
We need to engage, we
have to try to fight this,

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:10.237
and you were completely disengaged.

00:05:10.237 --> 00:05:11.760
It was like--

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:13.070
I'd settled in.
You had completely

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:14.970
settled in, you were like--

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:17.430
See, I'd do well in prison.

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:19.030
Well you do well--
I make myself right at home.

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:20.480
You do well in golf prison.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.240
You do well in golf prison, but--

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:27.790
Did it have golf course accoutrements?

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:29.670
No it was--
Or was there like--

00:05:29.670 --> 00:05:32.110
It was like, well, I'll explain it.

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:34.423
It was almost like it was just a building.

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:38.070
Maybe with a gate.
Low security.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:41.933
Like a medium to low
security prison for murder.

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:43.863
And--

00:05:43.863 --> 00:05:45.420
Who did I kill supposedly?

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:47.580
I don't have the details of the murder.

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:48.730
It didn't register with me,

00:05:48.730 --> 00:05:49.980
I just knew that you were innocent

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:51.230
and I was like I gotta
talk to Link about this

00:05:51.230 --> 00:05:52.700
but when I began talking to you about it,

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:57.040
again, you were not responsive to the idea

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:59.420
of challenging this.
Was I dejected

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:00.490
or was I happy?

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:02.290
What was my state?

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:04.959
You were indifferent, you were disengaged

00:06:04.959 --> 00:06:07.070
and I was very mad.

00:06:07.070 --> 00:06:08.360
I was very upset with you.

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:12.470
Yeah 'cause I did wanna get
into also your emotional state

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:14.820
'cause I think this could be revealing.

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:18.850
So before I made you angry,
what was your emotional state?

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:21.170
Were you crying or were you--

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:22.890
The beginning of the dream at least as far

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:25.750
as I remember was I am at golf prison

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:29.658
and I've gotta figure this out,

00:06:29.658 --> 00:06:31.140
I gotta get Link out of here.

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:33.450
It was just very much just that was it

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:35.240
and then I go in there
and start talking to you

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:38.343
in the area where you
can talk to prisoners.

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:41.856
You have on an orange shirt,

00:06:41.856 --> 00:06:43.170
orange jumpsuit.
Was there--

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:44.437
No I'm saying--
Was there glass?

00:06:44.437 --> 00:06:45.850
I'm sitting at a table with you.

00:06:45.850 --> 00:06:47.020
Okay.

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:48.310
And--
But no touching.

00:06:48.310 --> 00:06:51.420
And I was like hey man,
you didn't do this.

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:52.990
We gotta get your story out there

00:06:52.990 --> 00:06:55.010
and you just weren't saying anything.

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:56.500
You were kinda just looking at me like

00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:58.100
why are you so upset about this?

00:06:58.987 --> 00:07:03.750
So then, the door opens.

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:04.583
Oh.

00:07:04.583 --> 00:07:06.300
And I'm like this isn't just the door

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:07.530
to the room opens and there's a hall,

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:09.650
no the door opens and there's just woods.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:10.820
It's like--
Oh yeah.

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:12.670
Not a well designed prison.

00:07:12.670 --> 00:07:14.610
The door opens and we can totally get out.

00:07:14.610 --> 00:07:16.755
Was there music and a special light like

00:07:16.755 --> 00:07:17.850
♪ Ah ♪

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:19.740
That doesn't happen in my dreams.

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:23.193
So I looked at you and
I was like let's go.

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:28.220
Because what was happening in my brain was

00:07:29.190 --> 00:07:31.290
we gotta go through this
long legal procedure

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:32.440
to get him out.

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:33.810
He's not even on board.

00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:35.660
Were you thinking about content?

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:36.820
Were you thinking about our careers

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:39.110
or were you just thinking
about our friendship?

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:41.390
I really need to know, Rhett.

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:43.450
I can make up an answer.

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:44.283
Be honest.
That would make you feel

00:07:44.283 --> 00:07:45.116
a certain way.
No.

00:07:45.116 --> 00:07:46.476
No no I'm saying I don't know.

00:07:46.476 --> 00:07:48.175
Oh, oh.
It's a dream.

00:07:48.175 --> 00:07:50.990
It's a fragmented reality,
you know what I'm saying.

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:52.920
It was probably all wrapped up together.

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:54.230
So--
I was probably thinking

00:07:54.230 --> 00:07:55.470
like prison content.

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:58.730
The funny thing is is as you...

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:03.310
It took you a second to
be like okay I'm gonna go

00:08:03.310 --> 00:08:05.640
but you ran out after me.

00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:08.741
And my old Dodge Intrepid that I drove

00:08:08.741 --> 00:08:10.640
at the end of high
school and the beginning

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:12.150
of college was the car that I was driving

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:15.670
because that's how these
things happen in dreams.

00:08:15.670 --> 00:08:20.060
And I just get into the
Intrepid and start driving

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:22.242
and you are running after the Intrepid.

00:08:22.242 --> 00:08:23.920
Like catching a train?

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:26.260
So in other words, I'm
running away without the guy

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:27.393
that I'm trying to get out of prison.

00:08:27.393 --> 00:08:28.860
It's like where am I going?

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:31.510
I just visited prison, I don't
have to leave in a hurry.

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:34.290
It seemed that I had a motivation issue

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:38.150
so you really needed to,
needed to get me off the dime.

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:40.290
Then you're running next to the car

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:42.830
and then I'm like get into the car.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:45.230
And you're like but my shirt is messed up.

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:46.300
What?

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:49.723
And I look and the sleeves
of your orange jumpsuit

00:08:49.723 --> 00:08:53.630
are detached and you've taped them on

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:56.682
and you're trying to get the tape right.

00:08:56.682 --> 00:08:57.710
That's important.

00:08:57.710 --> 00:08:59.148
Can't get into a getaway vehicle--

00:08:59.148 --> 00:09:00.047
And I'm like--
If your sleeves

00:09:00.047 --> 00:09:01.350
are not perfect.

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:04.017
I'm like don't worry about the jumpsuit!

00:09:04.017 --> 00:09:05.731
Get in the Intrepid!

00:09:05.731 --> 00:09:09.540
Ironically it would have been
better to shed the jumpsuit.

00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:11.831
You don't wanna be driving around town

00:09:11.831 --> 00:09:14.897
in an Intrepid with a prison uniform on.

00:09:14.897 --> 00:09:19.090
Did it have golf insignias
or anything on it?

00:09:19.090 --> 00:09:20.040
No golf relation.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:21.650
There was nothing related to golf.

00:09:21.650 --> 00:09:22.530
Did I get in?

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:24.140
You got in.

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:27.970
We start driving down
that part of the circle

00:09:27.970 --> 00:09:29.412
in Keith Hills and we're driving

00:09:29.412 --> 00:09:33.480
towards Wiggin's old house,
coming around that way.

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:34.403
The big house.

00:09:35.243 --> 00:09:36.770
Well I guess prison's a big house

00:09:36.770 --> 00:09:37.603
but he had a large house.

00:09:37.603 --> 00:09:40.840
And apparently the security
response is incredibly quick

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:42.810
'cause literally we've been out of prison

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:44.920
for 17 seconds and there's already cops

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:46.873
with teams of dogs--
Wow.

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:51.760
Cops with teams of dogs
coming through the yards

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:54.160
along all the houses
right there on the river.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:55.050
Just coming out of the woodwork.

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:56.220
And we just drive by them.

00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:57.870
Slow?

00:09:57.870 --> 00:09:59.386
Yeah, we didn't wanna draw any attention.

00:09:59.386 --> 00:10:00.390
Just keep it cool.
I wanted to make sure

00:10:00.390 --> 00:10:02.210
they saw your orange sleeves.

00:10:03.265 --> 00:10:05.050
That guy's sleeves are in tact.

00:10:05.050 --> 00:10:06.950
Well they're taped a little bit, nah,

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:08.060
doesn't seem suspicious.

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:11.448
Now and as is the case
with a lot of dreams

00:10:11.448 --> 00:10:15.210
that reach a real point
of excitement like that,

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:17.020
I woke up at that moment.

00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:18.290
You woke up.

00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:19.700
Then the weirdest thing happened.

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:21.103
Now this was Saturday night.

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:23.730
I ended up staying Saturday night

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:27.630
because Locke ended up
having some games in Anaheim,

00:10:27.630 --> 00:10:28.920
basketball games so I was like oh,

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:29.970
I've already got the hotel room,

00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:32.123
I'll just say at VidCon for another day.

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:37.100
So this dream woke me up at

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:40.116
about five o'clock in the morning.

00:10:40.116 --> 00:10:41.240
Mm-hmm.

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:44.350
Now I had every reason and
intention to go back to sleep

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:49.590
but the thing that I could
not stop thinking about

00:10:49.590 --> 00:10:51.570
is how to get away from the cops.

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:53.627
While you were awake?
I was awake.

00:10:53.627 --> 00:10:56.415
And I was literally, I was
trying to go back to sleep

00:10:56.415 --> 00:10:58.190
and as I would go back to sleep,

00:10:58.190 --> 00:11:00.920
the thing that I would
almost begin dreaming about

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:02.500
was picking up the chase where it left off

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:05.523
and what I was gonna do, like
a choose your own adventure.

00:11:06.610 --> 00:11:08.350
And I went through all
these things, I was like,

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:12.740
well they're definitely
trying to drive out.

00:11:12.740 --> 00:11:14.755
There's only one way out of the gate.

00:11:14.755 --> 00:11:17.597
They're gonna have the gate
barricaded, we can't get out

00:11:17.597 --> 00:11:22.500
so what we should have done
is we should have gone down

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:23.980
to the river and I was like

00:11:23.980 --> 00:11:25.510
should we have crossed the river?

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:26.680
No 'cause they would find us,

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:28.940
they've got helicopters and
stuff and I was like no,

00:11:28.940 --> 00:11:30.960
what we should have done,
'cause we should have waited

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:34.690
until it was night and
then we should have gotten

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:37.870
into a canoe and gone way down the river

00:11:37.870 --> 00:11:39.950
and then we should have
gotten out of the river

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:42.530
at one of those places
where there was a little hut

00:11:42.530 --> 00:11:44.760
for fishing and hunting
that sometimes people build

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:46.220
on the river.
Yeah.

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:49.120
And then let the boat
continue to go down the river

00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:52.473
so they'll find the boat
miles down the river

00:11:52.473 --> 00:11:55.147
and so they won't be
able, I thought about this

00:11:55.147 --> 00:11:56.393
for 45 minutes.
Might have thought we,

00:11:56.393 --> 00:11:59.920
that we did, you find
the canoe, it's broken up

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:02.184
on some rapids.
Oh they drowned, yeah.

00:12:02.184 --> 00:12:04.169
But really we're just livin' large

00:12:04.169 --> 00:12:05.860
in some little catfish hut.

00:12:05.860 --> 00:12:09.030
Could have taken off the
jumpsuit or at least the sleeves,

00:12:09.030 --> 00:12:12.410
put 'em in the river, like oh.

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:16.897
He either lost his arms,
his sleeves or he dissolved.

00:12:18.350 --> 00:12:20.050
Yeah you gotta throw some
articles of clothing--

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:21.517
So you were thinking all of this.

00:12:21.517 --> 00:12:24.360
Trying to go back to sleep,
not wanting to think it

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:26.020
but I was like if I don't
figure out the best way

00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:28.573
to get away from the
cops at the golf prison,

00:12:29.660 --> 00:12:31.410
I'm not gonna be able to get good sleep

00:12:31.410 --> 00:12:34.603
and when I figured out I
think it's canoeing at night,

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:37.110
then I was like okay and
I went back to sleep.

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:38.300
Haven't thought about it since.

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:40.840
I don't think we ever
actually canoed at night.

00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:42.330
Did we?

00:12:42.330 --> 00:12:45.130
Of all the canoeing that we
did on the Cape Fear River--

00:12:46.230 --> 00:12:47.550
No, I did a lot of--

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:48.383
I don't recall any night canoeing.

00:12:48.383 --> 00:12:50.930
A lot of night fishing, night fishing,

00:12:50.930 --> 00:12:53.330
and we did a lot of night river crossing.

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:54.163
Yeah.

00:12:54.163 --> 00:12:55.710
'Cause sometimes we would get down there

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:56.730
too late or whatever.

00:12:56.730 --> 00:12:58.550
It's dangerous to be, I mean you need

00:12:58.550 --> 00:13:00.660
to have a spotlight I would think in order

00:13:00.660 --> 00:13:05.280
to navigate any rapids or whatever.

00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:07.120
I also wonder is there,

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:09.810
I bet you there is a golf
prison somewhere in the world

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:12.233
and it's probably Sweden.

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:16.780
Isn't that where the
really posh prisons are?

00:13:16.780 --> 00:13:18.940
Is that one of the Scandinavian--

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:20.810
Scandinavian prisons in general are nice.

00:13:20.810 --> 00:13:23.140
Norwegian prisons are nice.

00:13:23.140 --> 00:13:25.653
Are golf courses nice in Scandinavia?

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:28.400
Why am I asking you?

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:29.717
I would think so, why would they be bad?

00:13:29.717 --> 00:13:31.500
'Cause it's cold.

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:33.793
It's icy, it gets snowy up there.

00:13:34.810 --> 00:13:36.123
But it's not always snowy.

00:13:37.160 --> 00:13:40.023
Under the snow there's a nice golf prison.

00:13:41.029 --> 00:13:44.430
It only opens in the summer
and then in the winter,

00:13:44.430 --> 00:13:49.430
we send the prisoners to
the ski resort prison.

00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:51.450
That's what they do.

00:13:51.450 --> 00:13:52.840
I don't know how it works.

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:53.693
But if I am ever gonna kill somebody,

00:13:53.693 --> 00:13:55.620
it will be in Scandinavia.

00:13:55.620 --> 00:13:57.693
I do think if I went to prison,

00:14:01.370 --> 00:14:04.490
our working relation, this
is how it would play out.

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:06.445
You would have to do all the thinking.

00:14:06.445 --> 00:14:09.630
I mean, I'm not gonna sit

00:14:09.630 --> 00:14:12.837
in there like the Hurricane and try

00:14:12.837 --> 00:14:17.837
to figure out my own defense
and start writing letters to--

00:14:18.043 --> 00:14:19.570
I see that.
To advocates

00:14:19.570 --> 00:14:21.928
who can come in and get me out of prison.

00:14:21.928 --> 00:14:23.620
You'll just be like well--

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:25.210
Well.
This is just how it is man.

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:26.250
Don't worry so much about it.

00:14:26.250 --> 00:14:29.363
I've already started etching
how many days I'm here

00:14:29.363 --> 00:14:33.280
on my cell and I've started
way up here in the corner.

00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:35.460
So I don't wanna run out of space.

00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:36.700
I'd be thinking things like that.

00:14:36.700 --> 00:14:37.533
Right.

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:40.320
You gotta think strategic.

00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:43.717
You don't wanna start
etching the days on your cell

00:14:43.717 --> 00:14:45.910
right in the middle and
then what are you gonna do,

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:47.080
a spiral pattern?

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:51.617
No you gotta start in an
upper right-hand corner.

00:14:51.617 --> 00:14:52.750
I don't think they let you do that anymore

00:14:52.750 --> 00:14:53.960
and I also don't think it's necessary

00:14:53.960 --> 00:14:56.800
'cause I think you just ask
the guard what's the date

00:14:56.800 --> 00:14:58.080
and he just tells you.

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:01.680
Or you ask your caddy at the golf prison.

00:15:01.680 --> 00:15:05.633
It's like how many yards to my release?

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:09.390
Do I need a three iron to get out of here?

00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:10.890
Is that a thing, a three iron?

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:13.563
No three iron is a thing, yeah.

00:15:13.563 --> 00:15:14.933
It's nine irons.

00:15:17.670 --> 00:15:18.953
I wonder how it would impact the prison.

00:15:18.953 --> 00:15:21.370
Is that true, are there nine irons?

00:15:21.370 --> 00:15:24.880
Well it just depends on
what bag you're in but yeah.

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:28.170
Nine iron is the highest numbered iron.

00:15:28.170 --> 00:15:29.780
Okay, see, I know stuff.

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:32.780
There are as many as three or four irons

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:37.780
of increasing waft above that
that are called pitching wedge

00:15:38.530 --> 00:15:41.940
and sand wedge and lock
wedge and gap wedge

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:43.123
and things like that.

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:46.520
And then some people like
my father and me by the way,

00:15:46.520 --> 00:15:49.370
we don't play with a three iron,

00:15:49.370 --> 00:15:51.170
we play with a three hybrid.

00:15:51.170 --> 00:15:53.460
It's for people who need
a little bit more help

00:15:53.460 --> 00:15:56.900
because it's hard to hit those long irons.

00:15:56.900 --> 00:15:58.510
These are the kinda
conversations I'm having

00:15:58.510 --> 00:15:59.660
in prison by the way.

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:00.800
Well I'm gonna teach--

00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:02.662
I'm a gang leader, I'm a golf gang leader.

00:16:02.662 --> 00:16:04.340
I'm gonna teach golf in golf prison.

00:16:04.340 --> 00:16:06.220
Oh that's your in.

00:16:06.220 --> 00:16:07.870
That's how I get into the prison.

00:16:07.870 --> 00:16:10.250
Then you're sneaking over there
and digging a hole for me.

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:11.890
With a three iron 'cause I don't use it,

00:16:11.890 --> 00:16:14.023
I might use it to hit a golf ball with.

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:16.370
Christy and I--
The shovel.

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:18.710
Christy and I got in a
little kerfuffle about

00:16:18.710 --> 00:16:22.070
in the wake of the earthquakes
and we were talking

00:16:22.070 --> 00:16:25.350
about the dynamic of
why she's gathering all

00:16:25.350 --> 00:16:29.393
this earthquake stuff and
ordering it and I was like,

00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:32.970
she's baffled by my...

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:36.900
Just like I was acting in golf prison,

00:16:36.900 --> 00:16:39.730
just kinda, okay, it'll be fine.

00:16:39.730 --> 00:16:41.450
If I ignore the fact I'm in golf prison

00:16:41.450 --> 00:16:42.633
I think it'll be okay.

00:16:43.970 --> 00:16:45.113
And I'm like--

00:16:45.113 --> 00:16:47.153
Where's that come from?

00:16:47.153 --> 00:16:49.143
I don't know, I think it's--

00:16:49.143 --> 00:16:50.593
It's your coping mechanism.

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:55.440
I don't know what the word
is, if it's codependency

00:16:55.440 --> 00:16:58.650
or if it's just laziness
but when you were ordering

00:16:58.650 --> 00:17:02.559
all that apocalypse
stuff and I was like hey,

00:17:02.559 --> 00:17:04.650
can you just double your order?

00:17:04.650 --> 00:17:07.640
You graciously did and
I felt good about that.

00:17:07.640 --> 00:17:09.470
It feels good knowing that
someone else is worrying

00:17:09.470 --> 00:17:12.767
about it and I said,
"Christy it's not that

00:17:12.767 --> 00:17:17.373
"I don't think it's valid,
it's that I think that,

00:17:18.417 --> 00:17:21.647
"I trust you, I know
that you're very attuned

00:17:21.647 --> 00:17:25.337
"to the dangers associated
with it and being prepared

00:17:25.337 --> 00:17:26.660
"as much as possible."

00:17:26.660 --> 00:17:29.170
So I know I don't have
to worry about that.

00:17:29.170 --> 00:17:32.910
I have this, to a fault, I
have this heightened sense

00:17:32.910 --> 00:17:37.910
of brain power allocation.

00:17:38.550 --> 00:17:42.150
And if I start allocating
brain power to earthquake

00:17:42.150 --> 00:17:44.960
or apocalypse preparedness,
that's less I've got

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:46.977
to allocate towards something else like

00:17:46.977 --> 00:17:50.260
perfectly optimizing our vacation plans.

00:17:50.260 --> 00:17:53.310
So that was my response
to Christy, I was like,

00:17:53.310 --> 00:17:54.920
you got this, girl.

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:57.130
And I got this, girl.

00:17:57.130 --> 00:18:02.130
So let's not, there's no
implied judgment here,

00:18:02.380 --> 00:18:05.720
but it does make me look a
little stupid where it's like--

00:18:05.720 --> 00:18:07.663
You looked pretty stupid
in the dream, yeah.

00:18:09.130 --> 00:18:11.510
Well I think it was the sleeves.

00:18:11.510 --> 00:18:12.343
It was the sleeves.
They didn't help.

00:18:12.343 --> 00:18:13.430
I mean they were taped.

00:18:13.430 --> 00:18:14.290
You shouldn't have taped 'em.

00:18:14.290 --> 00:18:16.610
You should have just gone
sleeveless because that's a look

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:18.290
that I think would work in golf prison.

00:18:18.290 --> 00:18:20.040
Right, you really assert yourself.

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:22.070
Has there ever been a
golfer and I'm not talking

00:18:22.070 --> 00:18:22.903
about in prison--

00:18:22.903 --> 00:18:24.105
I think it's--
Sleeveless?

00:18:24.105 --> 00:18:25.590
I think it's against the dress code.

00:18:25.590 --> 00:18:27.150
They got a dress code?

00:18:27.150 --> 00:18:28.828
Yeah I think--
Golf and tennis,

00:18:28.828 --> 00:18:31.290
they need to loosen up.

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:33.213
You have to have your shirt tucked in.

00:18:34.571 --> 00:18:36.080
I don't know.
Basketball players have

00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:37.263
to tuck their shirt in but I think

00:18:37.263 --> 00:18:39.380
that there's something to do with safety.

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:41.917
I think it's just respecting the game.

00:18:41.917 --> 00:18:42.800
And defense.
It's really just respect.

00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:44.830
You don't have to wear--
It's control.

00:18:44.830 --> 00:18:46.913
Well you don't, and I think Tiger was--

00:18:46.913 --> 00:18:49.747
It's old farts trying to seem like they--

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:53.690
Well no, I don't necessarily think so.

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:55.970
I think it's just, it's a tradition

00:18:55.970 --> 00:18:58.540
but I think Tiger wears
that mock turtleneck

00:18:58.540 --> 00:19:02.360
a lot of times, he wears red on Sunday.

00:19:02.360 --> 00:19:04.040
And that's pushing the limits?

00:19:04.040 --> 00:19:08.080
I don't recall specifically
but my guess is

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:09.890
is that it must have been controversial

00:19:09.890 --> 00:19:13.182
when he decided to wear
that the first time.

00:19:13.182 --> 00:19:14.480
It's like oh he doesn't have a collar.

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:16.110
Maybe there was a
discussion about the rules

00:19:16.110 --> 00:19:18.140
at that point, I don't
know, somebody look that up.

00:19:18.140 --> 00:19:20.860
His shirt doesn't button and it creeps up

00:19:20.860 --> 00:19:22.560
to the bottom of his Adam's apple.

00:19:22.560 --> 00:19:24.490
It's almost a turtleneck
but it kinda feels like

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:27.100
it's just pretending to be a turtleneck.

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:29.500
Let's call it a mock turtleneck.

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:30.780
Okay well that's not what
we're gonna talk about.

00:19:30.780 --> 00:19:33.817
We're not gonna talk anymore
about golf and turtlenecks

00:19:33.817 --> 00:19:35.890
and prison or golf
prison, we're gonna talk

00:19:35.890 --> 00:19:37.500
about whether or not we're too nice

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:40.130
and how that relates
to some personal things

00:19:40.130 --> 00:19:42.563
and also some professional things.

00:19:43.440 --> 00:19:45.770
But first we wanna let you know,

00:19:45.770 --> 00:19:46.850
you think you can grab that pin?

00:19:46.850 --> 00:19:48.250
You think you can reach
all the way and grab that?

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:49.083
Yeah.

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:51.160
You ready?
Yeah.

00:19:52.230 --> 00:19:53.690
Look at that.

00:19:53.690 --> 00:19:58.433
This is the Mythical Society
pin, Semper Curiosus.

00:19:59.360 --> 00:20:00.980
Which second and third tier members

00:20:00.980 --> 00:20:03.960
of the Mythical Society
got when they signed up.

00:20:03.960 --> 00:20:05.656
We're making it available

00:20:05.656 --> 00:20:07.590
to everyone in the Mythical Society.

00:20:07.590 --> 00:20:09.530
I didn't say, you thought
I was gonna say everyone.

00:20:09.530 --> 00:20:11.450
Everyone in the Mythical Society

00:20:11.450 --> 00:20:13.880
at Mythical.store but you're gonna be,

00:20:13.880 --> 00:20:15.620
at the Mythical Store,
there's going to be--

00:20:15.620 --> 00:20:17.070
For purchase.

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:19.890
A code that you can,

00:20:19.890 --> 00:20:22.730
I don't exactly know how it is
but if you're on the Society,

00:20:22.730 --> 00:20:27.510
you will know how to get to
the listing at Mythical.store

00:20:27.510 --> 00:20:28.660
and then how to buy it.

00:20:30.240 --> 00:20:31.343
Cool little pin.

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:34.800
Check out the Mythical Society.

00:20:34.800 --> 00:20:35.633
Sign up.

00:20:37.285 --> 00:20:39.440
I guarantee you'll love it.

00:20:39.440 --> 00:20:41.270
Wow that's quite a guarantee.

00:20:41.270 --> 00:20:43.940
If you don't you can always quit it but

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:46.095
I betcha that won't happen.

00:20:46.095 --> 00:20:48.170
That's your right though.

00:20:48.170 --> 00:20:50.890
This pin is really cool
and we got other cool pins

00:20:51.790 --> 00:20:53.410
on the Mythical Store.

00:20:53.410 --> 00:20:55.530
That Cotton Candy Randy pin, man.

00:20:55.530 --> 00:20:56.870
I've seen some pictures of that thing

00:20:56.870 --> 00:21:00.200
and his legs are gonna jump
out and whisper in your ear.

00:21:00.200 --> 00:21:01.650
It's a great design.
Yeah.

00:21:02.600 --> 00:21:04.113
Mythical.store.

00:21:05.470 --> 00:21:06.593
Are we too nice?

00:21:08.864 --> 00:21:13.864
I really don't know where
this conversation's gonna go.

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:17.700
Maybe we can tee it up with...

00:21:19.490 --> 00:21:22.740
It is true that we do
find ourselves asking

00:21:22.740 --> 00:21:24.530
that question at times.

00:21:24.530 --> 00:21:26.090
There's different ways to look at this.

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:27.490
I'm gonna let you start in where you want.

00:21:27.490 --> 00:21:29.660
I'm just kinda setting the table.

00:21:29.660 --> 00:21:34.660
'Cause I think that
there's our public persona,

00:21:34.720 --> 00:21:37.760
like part of our brain
is that we're nice guys.

00:21:37.760 --> 00:21:40.510
But I'd like to, so we can explore that.

00:21:40.510 --> 00:21:42.640
And it's not just public, it's,

00:21:42.640 --> 00:21:44.020
I do like to believe that it's private.

00:21:44.020 --> 00:21:48.160
And then obviously we can
explore the personal nature

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:52.520
of yeah, I think we're nice guys.

00:21:52.520 --> 00:21:54.110
Well my most--
Not 'cause we're southern.

00:21:54.110 --> 00:21:56.039
Is that just--
I think it's part of it.

00:21:56.039 --> 00:21:57.363
What are the reasons?

00:21:58.370 --> 00:22:01.180
We talked at some point
about our conflict avoidance

00:22:01.180 --> 00:22:04.253
and how that was sort of
a deeply southern thing.

00:22:05.138 --> 00:22:07.570
I think some of it is related to that

00:22:07.570 --> 00:22:09.920
and for me the most interesting aspect

00:22:09.920 --> 00:22:13.400
of this conversation is professionally

00:22:14.410 --> 00:22:17.430
and how it relates to
our content but I do,

00:22:17.430 --> 00:22:20.953
because it's so fresh, I
do and it's very relevant,

00:22:22.420 --> 00:22:25.567
I wanna tell the story that
happened before my dream

00:22:25.567 --> 00:22:27.820
and was probably the
meal that I was digesting

00:22:27.820 --> 00:22:29.550
when I had my dream.
Okay.

00:22:29.550 --> 00:22:31.590
Which is a Saturday night
dinner with my family.

00:22:31.590 --> 00:22:33.990
Now I've never taken my
entire family to VidCon.

00:22:34.845 --> 00:22:37.479
And this was the first time
that that had happened.

00:22:37.479 --> 00:22:39.480
They came in a little bit late

00:22:39.480 --> 00:22:42.810
and it turns out Locke had
a couple of basketball games

00:22:42.810 --> 00:22:44.283
in Anaheim that we had
to stick around for,

00:22:44.283 --> 00:22:46.270
I think I already said this.

00:22:46.270 --> 00:22:49.174
Just told os many people
now, I'm repeating things.

00:22:49.174 --> 00:22:52.850
But so we spent the
night on Saturday night

00:22:52.850 --> 00:22:55.438
and we were gonna go grab some dinner

00:22:55.438 --> 00:22:57.740
and I was like, we should do something

00:22:57.740 --> 00:23:01.013
that's not super close to
VidCon because there'll be

00:23:01.013 --> 00:23:03.830
a bunch of people from VidCon

00:23:03.830 --> 00:23:05.910
and technically you're not
even really supposed to,

00:23:05.910 --> 00:23:08.233
we're not supposed to be out
and about anywhere near VidCon,

00:23:08.233 --> 00:23:10.660
it's a security concern, right,

00:23:10.660 --> 00:23:12.985
so they don't even let us do it.

00:23:12.985 --> 00:23:15.570
And if you do, that's another night

00:23:15.570 --> 00:23:16.980
where you have to be nice.

00:23:16.980 --> 00:23:19.130
You have to manufacture niceness for fans.

00:23:19.130 --> 00:23:19.963
Right.

00:23:20.821 --> 00:23:21.700
Because you're so mean in real life

00:23:21.700 --> 00:23:23.080
which we'll get to later.

00:23:23.080 --> 00:23:26.050
And so you know that restaurant Roy's?

00:23:26.050 --> 00:23:28.100
There's one in Pasadena.

00:23:28.100 --> 00:23:30.110
It's a Hawaiian place.

00:23:30.110 --> 00:23:31.330
Never heard of it.

00:23:31.330 --> 00:23:34.720
I've seen it around, it's a
chain that I think is not,

00:23:34.720 --> 00:23:36.160
it doesn't' go outside of California.

00:23:36.160 --> 00:23:38.190
Maybe it does, I don't know.

00:23:38.190 --> 00:23:41.430
But we wanted to go there.

00:23:41.430 --> 00:23:42.383
A Hawaiian restaurant?

00:23:42.383 --> 00:23:44.364
It's a Hawaiian steakhouse,

00:23:44.364 --> 00:23:46.960
like a upscale Hawaiian restaurant.

00:23:46.960 --> 00:23:47.793
Okay.

00:23:47.793 --> 00:23:50.183
So not like a Hawaiian
barbecue strip mall situation.

00:23:51.370 --> 00:23:54.150
And I was like okay let's go there

00:23:54.150 --> 00:23:57.590
and didn't realize that
it was actually very close

00:23:57.590 --> 00:24:00.010
to the convention center, it
was far away from the hotel

00:24:00.010 --> 00:24:01.287
but it was close to the convention center

00:24:01.287 --> 00:24:03.457
and so I got a little bit
nervous as we're pulling up.

00:24:03.457 --> 00:24:06.980
It was kinda late, I
was like there might be,

00:24:06.980 --> 00:24:10.040
so then as we're driving, it's
sort of like an outdoor mall

00:24:10.040 --> 00:24:12.690
kind of area, I do see a lot
of lanyards and I'm like,

00:24:12.690 --> 00:24:14.430
ah this is kind of a VidCon crowd

00:24:14.430 --> 00:24:16.820
and we had just done our meet and greet,

00:24:16.820 --> 00:24:19.710
and not that I don't have a,
I was actually just worried

00:24:19.710 --> 00:24:23.010
about kinda violating the rules honestly.

00:24:23.010 --> 00:24:25.240
But I was also like
the kids had been here,

00:24:25.240 --> 00:24:26.650
I haven't spent a lot of time with them

00:24:26.650 --> 00:24:29.090
and I kinda wanna just go
have a nice dinner with them.

00:24:29.090 --> 00:24:32.120
So I told Jessie as we were
pulling into the parking garage,

00:24:32.120 --> 00:24:34.030
I was like I'm gonna do the
thing that we talked about

00:24:34.030 --> 00:24:36.350
on a previous--
The Sterling K Brown.

00:24:36.350 --> 00:24:37.873
Sterling K Brown, we just
call it the Sterling K Brown.

00:24:39.662 --> 00:24:42.192
That is what it is.

00:24:42.192 --> 00:24:46.790
And that is when if approached,
you say I'm with my family,

00:24:46.790 --> 00:24:48.810
I'm sorry, if somebody wants a picture

00:24:48.810 --> 00:24:50.100
or somebody wants an
autograph or whatever,

00:24:50.100 --> 00:24:52.400
you just say I'm sorry,
I'm with my family.

00:24:52.400 --> 00:24:53.960
And that's a very difficult thing,

00:24:53.960 --> 00:24:55.440
I don't know if you've instituted that,

00:24:55.440 --> 00:24:56.870
how many times you've instituted that,

00:24:56.870 --> 00:24:58.770
it's a very difficult thing for me to do

00:24:58.770 --> 00:25:02.140
because I am a nice guy, right?

00:25:02.140 --> 00:25:05.360
And also for all the
reasons that we talked about

00:25:05.360 --> 00:25:08.726
in the past, I feel a
sense of obligation to fans

00:25:08.726 --> 00:25:11.623
to be nice and give them a moment.

00:25:12.920 --> 00:25:17.070
Now, so I go in but I'm like
I'm gonna hold to this, guys.

00:25:17.070 --> 00:25:19.176
I was like I'm gonna do
the Sterling K Brown.

00:25:20.380 --> 00:25:22.540
We get out of the, and
everybody's on board,

00:25:22.540 --> 00:25:25.293
family's on board seemingly at the time.

00:25:26.620 --> 00:25:29.550
We get out of the car,
we go to the elevator

00:25:29.550 --> 00:25:31.420
that is gonna--
Roy got a elevator?

00:25:31.420 --> 00:25:33.480
No no it was like there was a parking deck

00:25:33.480 --> 00:25:34.890
and then it was an outdoor
mall so you gotta go

00:25:34.890 --> 00:25:36.980
from the parking deck up to the--

00:25:36.980 --> 00:25:38.540
Like dang.

00:25:38.540 --> 00:25:40.890
Roy doesn't have an
elevator that I know of.

00:25:40.890 --> 00:25:44.000
And we're getting ready
to get on the elevator.

00:25:44.000 --> 00:25:46.980
My dad has an elevator in his beach house.

00:25:46.980 --> 00:25:48.400
That's cool.

00:25:48.400 --> 00:25:49.233
Just bragging a little.

00:25:49.233 --> 00:25:51.800
And a woman--
His house is on stilts.

00:25:51.800 --> 00:25:54.893
A mom and a little girl,

00:25:56.000 --> 00:25:59.250
probably 12.
Immediate test.

00:25:59.250 --> 00:26:02.370
Come up, now, I recognize at least the mom

00:26:02.370 --> 00:26:04.870
but I think both of them
from the meet and greet.

00:26:04.870 --> 00:26:06.920
They had just been in the meet and greet.

00:26:08.820 --> 00:26:11.020
I have thoughts but go ahead.

00:26:11.020 --> 00:26:12.390
But I kinda didn't remember that

00:26:12.390 --> 00:26:15.315
until after they went away
to be honest with you.

00:26:15.315 --> 00:26:18.310
I was like oh crap, they
were at the meet and greet.

00:26:18.310 --> 00:26:20.580
250 people, you can't remember everybody.

00:26:20.580 --> 00:26:22.019
I bet they remembered it.

00:26:22.019 --> 00:26:25.870
So I said, she comes up and she's like,

00:26:25.870 --> 00:26:28.670
I saw them looking at me
and I was like here we go.

00:26:28.670 --> 00:26:32.097
Little girl comes up, she's
got a bag and she's like,

00:26:32.097 --> 00:26:34.190
"Would you please sign this?"

00:26:34.190 --> 00:26:37.070
And when you say here we
go, you're like here we go,

00:26:37.070 --> 00:26:39.070
this is a test in front of my family

00:26:39.070 --> 00:26:41.780
if I'm gonna Sterling K Brown this moment.

00:26:41.780 --> 00:26:42.613
Yeah.

00:26:42.613 --> 00:26:44.760
Okay, she had the bag.

00:26:44.760 --> 00:26:46.870
She says, "Will you please sign this?"

00:26:46.870 --> 00:26:48.893
And what's the family
configuration at this point

00:26:48.893 --> 00:26:50.940
because I think that's important.

00:26:50.940 --> 00:26:52.645
It's four people in my family.

00:26:52.645 --> 00:26:53.478
I know who's in your,

00:26:53.478 --> 00:26:55.110
I mean physically where are they standing?

00:26:55.110 --> 00:26:56.870
We're all standing outside of an elevator

00:26:56.870 --> 00:26:58.330
waiting for it to open.

00:26:58.330 --> 00:26:59.163
Okay.

00:26:59.163 --> 00:27:02.860
And I will say that no
one else was around, okay?

00:27:02.860 --> 00:27:06.670
No one else was around but I
had literally in the car not--

00:27:06.670 --> 00:27:07.937
Just said--
30 seconds ago said,

00:27:07.937 --> 00:27:10.350
"I'm Sterling K Browning this situation."

00:27:10.350 --> 00:27:11.850
And I'm not going off of that.

00:27:13.020 --> 00:27:14.817
Little girl says, "Will
you please sign this?"

00:27:14.817 --> 00:27:17.884
And I was like, "I'm
sorry, I'm with my family."

00:27:17.884 --> 00:27:18.801
Oh, dude.

00:27:19.780 --> 00:27:20.833
Okay okay okay.

00:27:22.610 --> 00:27:27.540
She looks a little
upset, a little shocked,

00:27:27.540 --> 00:27:28.453
including the mom.

00:27:29.330 --> 00:27:31.351
But they were nice enough,
when you say family

00:27:31.351 --> 00:27:34.003
they're like okay and then
they kinda just went away.

00:27:35.350 --> 00:27:37.267
We get on the elevator, Shepherd says,

00:27:37.267 --> 00:27:38.814
"Dad, that was a little girl."

00:27:45.100 --> 00:27:45.933
I'm like...

00:27:48.400 --> 00:27:51.881
And then Locke's like, "Yeah
and nobody was around."

00:27:53.620 --> 00:27:56.253
I'm like I'm doing this for y'all!

00:27:58.060 --> 00:27:59.713
Why you gotta criticize me?

00:28:00.699 --> 00:28:02.350
Dang.

00:28:02.350 --> 00:28:04.117
Because if you would have
done it, you would have got

00:28:04.117 --> 00:28:08.740
on the elevator and you
imagined it playing out as

00:28:08.740 --> 00:28:11.086
you would have turned and said
hey, it was a little girl.

00:28:12.842 --> 00:28:14.360
And there was no one else around.

00:28:14.360 --> 00:28:16.950
Right, and I got so close
to doing it but I was like

00:28:16.950 --> 00:28:18.730
this is the first test.

00:28:18.730 --> 00:28:21.020
And you know what, and what else,

00:28:21.020 --> 00:28:22.930
and then what did they say?

00:28:22.930 --> 00:28:25.640
Well it continued of course
throughout the night.

00:28:25.640 --> 00:28:27.580
I just mean the assessment of that,

00:28:27.580 --> 00:28:31.098
was that the end of that or did
they say but you know what--

00:28:31.098 --> 00:28:33.000
No no no, I said you know what--

00:28:33.000 --> 00:28:34.140
We're glad you did it.
I feel bad.

00:28:34.140 --> 00:28:37.430
I probably should have called
an audible in that situation.

00:28:37.430 --> 00:28:38.263
No.

00:28:38.263 --> 00:28:39.200
I gotta read the environment better.

00:28:39.200 --> 00:28:40.033
No!

00:28:40.033 --> 00:28:41.340
But that requires too much thinking.

00:28:41.340 --> 00:28:43.194
No no no no no, listen--

00:28:43.194 --> 00:28:44.393
You think I was still right?

00:28:46.240 --> 00:28:47.470
Your boys--
I'm a nice guy.

00:28:47.470 --> 00:28:49.500
Your boys--
Too nice.

00:28:49.500 --> 00:28:52.080
I think they didn't
articulate what they felt

00:28:52.080 --> 00:28:55.940
which was prioritize, man.

00:28:55.940 --> 00:28:57.670
That's the point.

00:28:57.670 --> 00:29:01.060
And you know what, you
did the right thing.

00:29:01.060 --> 00:29:04.610
You did the nice thing,
you were nice to those

00:29:04.610 --> 00:29:06.933
that you love the most for once.

00:29:06.933 --> 00:29:08.041
Yeah yeah that's right.

00:29:10.277 --> 00:29:13.640
When we were walking the floor at VidCon,

00:29:13.640 --> 00:29:15.870
you asked if I've done the
Sterling K Brown thing.

00:29:15.870 --> 00:29:17.340
Oh yeah yeah yeah.

00:29:17.340 --> 00:29:19.890
And then I'll let you
continue with your story.

00:29:19.890 --> 00:29:22.090
I'm talking with Lily because it was,

00:29:22.090 --> 00:29:24.887
the Sterling K Brown thing
happened to Lily and Christy.

00:29:24.887 --> 00:29:27.183
It was like me going up to him saying,

00:29:29.027 --> 00:29:31.160
"My girls are big fans."

00:29:31.160 --> 00:29:33.750
And then he Sterling K Browned me

00:29:33.750 --> 00:29:36.100
and I gained so much
more respect for the guy

00:29:36.100 --> 00:29:37.330
who I already had so much for.

00:29:37.330 --> 00:29:38.250
Right.

00:29:38.250 --> 00:29:43.250
So Lily experienced being
on the non-receiving end

00:29:43.390 --> 00:29:46.980
of a Sterling K Brown personally and then,

00:29:46.980 --> 00:29:49.510
and we had had this discussion
about this can become

00:29:49.510 --> 00:29:51.350
a part of what I do.

00:29:51.350 --> 00:29:52.490
Yeah.
So we're walking around

00:29:52.490 --> 00:29:55.820
the convention floor when
it's just for creators

00:29:55.820 --> 00:30:00.070
and their families but
with a lot of creators

00:30:00.070 --> 00:30:01.810
and their families want to come up to us--

00:30:01.810 --> 00:30:03.350
Yeah.
And get pictures taken

00:30:03.350 --> 00:30:04.860
even in that environment.

00:30:04.860 --> 00:30:07.010
I actually checked in with
you as we were going out

00:30:07.010 --> 00:30:09.110
into the--
And Lily did first

00:30:09.110 --> 00:30:11.010
and she, as we're walking in she was like,

00:30:11.010 --> 00:30:15.000
Dad, are you gonna tell 'em,

00:30:15.000 --> 00:30:16.067
you gonna Sterling K Brown these people?

00:30:16.067 --> 00:30:18.040
We should call it SKB.

00:30:18.040 --> 00:30:20.330
SKB 'em?
Yeah.

00:30:20.330 --> 00:30:21.200
And I was like,

00:30:21.200 --> 00:30:23.580
I've already been
thinking about that, yes.

00:30:23.580 --> 00:30:26.040
Because they want to go to things,

00:30:26.040 --> 00:30:27.880
they're moving and then they turn around

00:30:27.880 --> 00:30:30.150
and I'm back taking a
picture with somebody

00:30:30.150 --> 00:30:31.950
and it is very frustrating.

00:30:31.950 --> 00:30:34.363
It's like a perfect place to SKB.

00:30:35.340 --> 00:30:37.670
And she asked me about
it and I was like, yeah,

00:30:37.670 --> 00:30:40.910
I'm gonna do that and then
it immediately happened.

00:30:40.910 --> 00:30:44.980
And I was like I'm here with
my family and I gestured

00:30:44.980 --> 00:30:48.220
and they were walking ahead
so it was actually perfect.

00:30:48.220 --> 00:30:49.640
You see how you're
holding me up right now?

00:30:49.640 --> 00:30:50.560
I'm trying to be with them.

00:30:50.560 --> 00:30:52.200
I can't even physically be with them.

00:30:52.200 --> 00:30:53.966
It's not like they're
standing there in an elevator

00:30:53.966 --> 00:30:56.730
thinking that I'm the
one making the mistake.

00:30:56.730 --> 00:30:58.220
Right.

00:30:58.220 --> 00:30:59.650
And it felt good.

00:30:59.650 --> 00:31:02.760
And I also did it there.
I saw Lily turn around

00:31:02.760 --> 00:31:05.750
and she heard me say it and
then I caught up with them

00:31:05.750 --> 00:31:07.670
and there was just a
little twinkle in the eye

00:31:07.670 --> 00:31:10.260
and no word needed to be
said and it was like okay,

00:31:10.260 --> 00:31:11.720
you know what--
Well my kids did not

00:31:11.720 --> 00:31:13.560
appreciate me in the same way.

00:31:13.560 --> 00:31:15.160
I think in their heart they might.

00:31:15.160 --> 00:31:17.670
Oh I mean, there's a little girl.

00:31:17.670 --> 00:31:19.440
All right just go back on it then.

00:31:19.440 --> 00:31:20.943
No I'm not going back on it.

00:31:21.994 --> 00:31:23.620
And I will say that--

00:31:23.620 --> 00:31:25.950
You kept doing it?

00:31:25.950 --> 00:31:27.593
Okay in the restaurant,

00:31:29.650 --> 00:31:32.200
in the restaurant, well, on
the way to the restaurant,

00:31:32.200 --> 00:31:34.060
somebody asked and I SKBed them

00:31:35.260 --> 00:31:38.750
and then in the restaurant,
there was a family

00:31:38.750 --> 00:31:41.924
that was sitting there and you could see

00:31:41.924 --> 00:31:44.200
the discussion begin to happen that's like

00:31:44.200 --> 00:31:45.800
when are we gonna go over there?

00:31:46.800 --> 00:31:51.770
They waited until our
desserts had come or whatever.

00:31:51.770 --> 00:31:52.880
We got through our meal.

00:31:52.880 --> 00:31:54.490
Okay.

00:31:54.490 --> 00:31:59.490
And I guess I just lost
heart by that point

00:31:59.700 --> 00:32:02.680
and they asked for a
picture and I was like okay,

00:32:02.680 --> 00:32:04.130
we can get a quick one.

00:32:04.130 --> 00:32:07.210
I probably said it in a
very unenthusiastic way

00:32:07.210 --> 00:32:08.043
which made them feel horrible.

00:32:08.043 --> 00:32:10.179
That sounded pretty unenthusiastic.

00:32:10.179 --> 00:32:13.033
Okay, we can get a quick one.

00:32:14.010 --> 00:32:18.010
At the end of VidCon,
I'm drained unlike any--

00:32:18.010 --> 00:32:20.990
I literally had just done
all of Saturday and we did

00:32:20.990 --> 00:32:22.030
the meet and greet--
Oh gosh.

00:32:22.030 --> 00:32:22.980
And then--
Yeah that's tough.

00:32:22.980 --> 00:32:26.483
You know, it does take,
'cause we do try to be there

00:32:26.483 --> 00:32:29.710
for people and be present
and some people have a story

00:32:29.710 --> 00:32:32.170
to tell that maybe we don't want people

00:32:32.170 --> 00:32:34.150
to not tell us something
if they've got something

00:32:34.150 --> 00:32:37.100
to say but unless you're a robot

00:32:37.100 --> 00:32:38.900
it's an emotionally draining experience

00:32:38.900 --> 00:32:41.760
and you're kinda just ready
to pull back from all that.

00:32:41.760 --> 00:32:44.580
Well if I may, I suggest that we skip

00:32:44.580 --> 00:32:48.800
from fan interactions to
other types of niceties

00:32:48.800 --> 00:32:51.560
because I thought, when you
were talking about Roy's,

00:32:51.560 --> 00:32:53.483
I thought you were
actually gonna talk about

00:32:53.483 --> 00:32:58.311
the most quintessential nicety
which is how was your meal?

00:32:58.311 --> 00:33:00.540
Oh yeah.
And I think that's another--

00:33:00.540 --> 00:33:01.500
We did a whole podcast on that.

00:33:01.500 --> 00:33:02.980
We did a whole podcast on that one

00:33:02.980 --> 00:33:05.820
so I don't wanna camp
out there but I think,

00:33:05.820 --> 00:33:10.820
I still cannot say, tow
the party line of niceness

00:33:11.130 --> 00:33:13.790
and say, 'cause here's the deal.

00:33:13.790 --> 00:33:17.203
The opposite of nice is not mean

00:33:17.203 --> 00:33:19.580
in this conversation.

00:33:19.580 --> 00:33:22.370
The opposite of nice is not being a jerk

00:33:22.370 --> 00:33:26.840
or being cold-hearted, the
opposite of nice is what?

00:33:26.840 --> 00:33:29.430
Well sometimes honesty.
Honesty.

00:33:29.430 --> 00:33:34.430
And it's so hard to do
it because you just,

00:33:35.150 --> 00:33:40.150
and I think if I'm totally
honest with myself now

00:33:40.530 --> 00:33:44.410
about being honest with
the waiter, it's like well,

00:33:44.410 --> 00:33:45.870
the meal wasn't that great.

00:33:45.870 --> 00:33:48.200
I was disappointed in the so and so.

00:33:48.200 --> 00:33:51.245
It automatically, the reason
why I don't like doing it

00:33:51.245 --> 00:33:54.763
is because it just makes you
seem like an entitled jerk.

00:33:55.620 --> 00:33:57.480
Kinda like talking about how you got fans

00:33:57.480 --> 00:33:59.170
and you don't wanna be nice to 'em.

00:33:59.170 --> 00:34:00.838
Well and--
That's the risk right?

00:34:00.838 --> 00:34:01.862
And I do think--
That's why we don't like

00:34:01.862 --> 00:34:02.695
talking about it.
And sometimes,

00:34:02.695 --> 00:34:05.120
and I'm sure we talked about
this when we talked about it

00:34:05.120 --> 00:34:07.350
but and sometimes it's just not worth it

00:34:07.350 --> 00:34:10.310
but I had this happen to me
when I was in North Carolina.

00:34:10.310 --> 00:34:12.998
We're at a restaurant, just Jessie and I,

00:34:12.998 --> 00:34:16.821
and it was one of those situations,

00:34:16.821 --> 00:34:19.240
it was a waterfront restaurant,
we're sitting there,

00:34:19.240 --> 00:34:21.752
and then about 10 minutes into,

00:34:21.752 --> 00:34:23.973
all we had was drinks at the time,

00:34:25.680 --> 00:34:27.017
the waiter comes up and he's like,

00:34:27.017 --> 00:34:29.190
"Would you guys like to
move closer to the water?"

00:34:29.190 --> 00:34:32.410
And again, it's very
difficult to not take that

00:34:32.410 --> 00:34:36.020
as like, is this because
